   significantly potentiated DOX-induced cytotoxicity, particularly in
   SH-SY5Y cells, suggesting a strong chemosensitizing effect. Molecular
   docking revealed that BA binds within the ALK active site with a
   moderate binding energy (-5.149 kcal/ mol), compared with crizotinib
   (-9.784 kcal/mol) and doxorubicin (-7.119 kcal/mol) supporting ALK as a
   potential molecular target. Overall, these findings highlight betulinic
   acid as a},
